$$<p>Taylor Swift will perform at the CMA Awards for the first time in 13 years, with the 60th annual ceremony set for Wednesday 18 November 2026 at Bridgestone Arena in Nashville. The Country Music Association and ABC confirmed the booking on Friday 13 November through Good Morning America, and the announcement immediately became the biggest story of this year's awards.</p>
<p>Swift is also nominated at this year's ceremony. Her song "I Knew It, I Knew You", written for the Disney and Pixar film Toy Story 5, is up for Single of the Year. It is her 26th career nomination at the CMA Awards and her first in four years. The song has also reached No. 1 on US country radio, the first of her songs to top that chart in 13 years.</p>
<p>The night will mark a full-circle moment for an artist who began her career in Nashville before becoming one of the biggest pop stars in the world. This year also marks the 20th anniversary of her self-titled debut album, and on 26 October 2026 she was inducted into the Nashville Songwriters Hall of Fame.</p>
<h2>Taylor Swift CMA Awards 2026 at a glance</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Event</th><td>60th CMA Awards</td></tr>
